Fixed and verified. Summary:

**Bug** — `src/import_merge.ts:7` compared URLs with strict string equality (`b.url === inc.url`), so `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` didn't match `https://example.com/a` and got appended as a duplicate entry.

**Fix** — The library already has `normalizeUrl` in `src/url_utils.ts` (lowercases hostname, strips tracking params, drops trailing slash on the bare path). I added a `urlKey()` helper in `import_merge.ts` that uses it, with a raw-string fallback when `new URL()` throws on unparseable input, and the duplicate check now compares `urlKey(b.url) === urlKey(inc.url)`. A matched incoming bookmark still merges into the existing entry (existing kept, tags unioned via Set); unmatched ones are appended unchanged.

**Verification** — Added `tests/import_merge.test.ts` with 5 tests (red first: hostname-case and tracking-param cases failed before the fix):
- hostname-case duplicate → merged, existing entry kept, tags unioned (exact repro from the bug report)
- tracking-param difference → recognized as duplicate (same class of latent bug, since `normalizeUrl` strips `utm_*`/`fbclid`)
- no match → appended unchanged
- unparseable URLs → no throw, exact-string fallback still dedupes
- inputs not mutated

`deno task test`: 8/8 pass (5 new + 3 pre-existing). `deno task check`: clean (the linter's TS5097 `.ts`-extension warning is a false positive in this Deno project — deno check accepts it, same as the pre-existing imports).


